// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row str_is_u8_slice_debug_quotes_bytes (tier 2, `run 3`). Logos's `str` IS `[u8]` (`&str` is `&[u8]`, an unregistered divergence in docs/spec/divergences.md), so a byte slice takes str's impls: `{:?}` on `&[u8]` prints the bytes as a quoted string.
// Logos: prints "hi" (quoted) and exits 3
// rustc: prints [104, 105] and exits 0 (rustc 1.98.1 --edition 2024)
// corpus: str and [u8] are one type; the same identity blocks `impl<T: Debug> Debug for [T]` (it took `{:?}` on `&str`, printing [97, 98, 99])
// fix hint: make `str` its own type, as Rust's — `&str` → `&[u8]` only through `as_bytes`, `impl … for str` one fact (retire obl_str_facts_' `&[u8]` twin), then add `impl<T: Debug> Debug for [T]`
package str_is_u8_slice_debug_quotes_bytes;
use logos.std.fmt;
use logos.mem.string;
fn main() -> i32 {
    let b: &[u8] = &[104u8, 105u8];
    let s: String = format!("{:?}", b);
    println!("{}", s);
    if s == String::from("[104, 105]") { return 0; }
    return 3;
}
